{
 "read": "2026-10-04",
 "method": "Corrections to the brands read from the products' names (research-brands-from-names.json and research-cleaning-brands.json), each to the maker its own name states, and to none where the name states none. Chedraui's products, named in Spanish noun first, were given the noun for their brand: Leche for Lala's milk, Shampoo for Head & Shoulders', Cerveza for Corona; each is corrected to the maker after the noun and its description, and to none for produce, meat and fish by the kilo and a loose tortilla. Save-On-Foods names a product \"Maker - Product\" and its produce \"Noun - Detail\", so its spinach, onions and oranges were given their own noun for a maker, as were Giant Tiger's and Smart & Final's unbranded produce (Carrots, Zucchini, Gala, Navel, Seedless, Wrapped, Sleeved): each is corrected to none. A maker's name of two words or more was cut to its first (Bumble for Bumble Bee, Dr. for Dr. Oetker, Old for Old Spice, General for General Mills, Robin for Robin Hood): each is corrected to the whole name. A maker spelled elsewhere in the lists keeps that spelling (Kellogg's, TRESemme, Corona). The original research files are left as they were read.",
